        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "785e4e62-4563-5b54-81fd-bfe074a63d3c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Elia Kazan, William Inge, David Amram, Zohra Lampert, Natalie Wood, Warren Beatty\n- Products: Splendor in the Grass, Let's Scare Jessica to Death, Alphabet City\n- Topics: film credits, acting roles, biography\n\nFacts:\n- Elia Kazan was born as Elias Kazantzoglou on September 7, 1909, and he died on September 28, 2003.\n- Elia Kazan was a Greek-American director, producer, writer, and actor, and The New York Times described him as one of the most honored and influential directors in Broadway and Hollywood history.\n- Zohra Lampert was born on May 13, 1937, and she is an American actress with roles in film, television, and stage.\n- Splendor in the Grass is a 1961 Technicolor drama film about a teenage girl dealing with sexual repression, love, and heartbreak.\n- Splendor in the Grass was written by William Inge, directed by Elia Kazan, and scored by jazz composer David Amram.\n- William Inge appears briefly in Splendor in the Grass as a Protestant clergyman and won an Oscar for the film's screenplay.\n- Zohra Lampert starred alongside Natalie Wood and Warren Beatty in Splendor in the Grass.\n- In the 1971 cult horror film Let's Scare Jessica to Death, Zohra Lampert played the title character.\n- In Alphabet City, Zohra Lampert plays Johnny's mother.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a8b99dba-0e7e-5e01-a721-1f3931f2d797",
